	abstract = {{\textless}pre{\textgreater}{\textless}!--StartFragment--{\textgreater}The use of Self-Organizing Map ({\textless}span{\textgreater}SOM{\textless}/span{\textgreater}) algorithm for feature extraction and dimensionality reduction applied to underwater object detection with Low Frequency Electromagnetic Waves is presented. Computer simulation is used to generate a direct model for the study region, and a Self Organizing Map Algorithm is used to fit the data and return a similar model, with smaller dimensionality and same characteristics. Results show that virtual sensors are created by the {\textless}span{\textgreater}SOM{\textless}/span{\textgreater} algorithm with consistent predictions, filling the resolution gap of the input data. These results are useful for fastening decision making algorithms by reducing the number of inputs to a group of significant data.{\textless}!--EndFragment--{\textgreater}{\textless}/pre{\textgreater}},
